#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:5
#: bc4d120a5c8d49dcbad4facd495e3df8
msgid "GSoC - Google Summer of Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:6
#: 00c8168078354de1859161a099126e00
msgid "Each year, ArduPilot participates in the `Google Summer of Code program <https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/>`__, encouraging students and others to contribute to the ArduPilot codebase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:8
#: c4dbc853d2304ae1a07dd6f6e77ae2a1
msgid "The development team includes experienced mentors who will help students make great contributions to ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:10
#: 9180d063d18a4cfa8cede2b9791ef185
msgid "To help you get started:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:12
#: 42093dc8569644779ba0cb8002f3a9c8
msgid "The `timeline for GSoC 2026 is here <https://developers.google.com/open-source/gsoc/timeline>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:13
#: 8b2ff0eebe1d45489cfc07ab18ce21d5
msgid "The :ref:`suggested projects list and previous year GSoC projects <gsoc-ideas-list>` is here. This is a list of our ideas of what would be good to work on, but we are open to other suggestions you make in your application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:15
#: c015913031b0485981f17afc683172b7
msgid "The purpose of GSoC is to help people become long-term contributors. We want people to stay in the community after the term."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:17
#: bc90e1367d1541eda301bdaa6c5347ed
msgid "The #GSOC channel in the `ArduPilot Discord server <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ is a good place to ask questions about our GSOC program, submit ideas for projects, etc. Mentors will respond to your posts in this GSoC channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:18
#: 0382ef9889af42fd973ec35e48d1b5e6
msgid "The :ref:`ArduPilot Wiki <ardupilot:home>` and, specifically, the :ref:`ArduPilot Developers Wiki <dev:home>` are good sources of information on ArduPilot and how to contribute to its code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:19
#: e097c24c301044a9aa46949cd78c25ba
msgid "The `ArduPilot Discuss Forum GSoC category <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/google-summer-of-code/131>`__ is for GSoC topics and should be cross-posted to the #GSoC Discord channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:20
#: bce50a8c5a6c4841b5643a6d6dbe7185
msgid "Check out the `Blog <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/blog>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:21
#: b5203737583144bf8e733fcfc136b5f7
msgid "Past conference talks are on the `ArduPilot YouTube channel <https://www.youtube.com/@ardupilot19/playlists>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:24
#: 5f0908e09104453da302d765609c47cf
msgid "Advice for proposals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:26
#: 0c3ec0263bc24debb007272a87df70cf
msgid "Please note that there are likely to be more students applying than the number of places Google allocates, so to improve your chances, please include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:28
#: ffd60615ab2c4c1988e67f69259075f8
msgid "Above all, we welcome folks already working with ArduPilot who have not yet submitted open-source contributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:29
#: 7cd0a77195234cd0b6ace6f2e38503f2
msgid "Information on how you would approach the project, what time you can put into it, and what you think you can achieve over the GSoC period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:30
#: 9fa53d98485945aa94bbb3f271abf992
msgid "Information on the tools you will need to complete the project, including demonstrated ability in the relevant programming language or environment, and details of past open-source projects you have contributed to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:31
#: 4ccbbea41e234071b8c319fb96d71bc3
msgid "Enthusiasm for your chosen project. The best projects stand on their own, regardless of GSoC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:32
#: 9d345058c54a41e7a56ffa86090e0ca8
msgid "A feature and development motivation: what is missing today and why it matters to the ArduPilot ecosystem and community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:33
#: cbbc9d035fbe4a4ab143f0e0a3068be9
msgid "A short note on what already exists in ArduPilot that can be used as a foundation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:34
#: a39671e590d84e6fbd0f9dd8e9bb5d45
msgid "A basic sketch of your proposed solution so we can see your current level of understanding of the codebase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:35
#: c69b24c56e0c45f9b147e5308e164f47
msgid "A working plan with a timeline, end goals, and stretch goals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:36
#: c369e4e155cc4a65938ca8fb56ea2c11
msgid "A plan for your continued involvement with ArduPilot even if the GSoC project is not selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:37
#: ce2b95f4d06441669a7ee4381d5b022f
msgid "Images, diagrams, or schematics that support your idea."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:38
#: 415f772125bd4bbd94bcd0fea6a202f7
msgid "Your education background, and your near-term career ambitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:39
#: 00d23be14c09430d917917994414c8ec
msgid "Recent relevant work history, including whether you are working this summer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:40
#: 9eaa71d8fd034bbb96b4791c3cad5fc3
msgid "Your availability for the term, where you will be located, and any holiday plans during the term."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:41
#: 5abc562e61f242e3a3203315aaf70067
msgid "Previous contributions to ArduPilot, related open-source work, or relevant community activity, with links or other evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:43
#: 5635517c277c4a6694c45be0a8ffd82b
msgid "Helpful resources:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:45
#: 559236d78b9a4f11b1c64e39987bb03d
msgid "`Learning the codebase <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/learning-the-ardupilot-codebase.html>`__: a short start for how the repo is organized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:46
#: fc7f62d8fb044c0fba19f02451ae471d
msgid "`ArduPilot SITL <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.html>`__: our simulation tool; help us improve the SITL documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:47
#: e02c94b5e738440c9e8b3f6f7cf0c715
msgid "`SITL with Gazebo <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/sitl-with-gazebo.html>`__: extend SITL to physics simulators, including the free and open-source Gazebo simulator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:48
#: 255c9ea16ea04aae948fc6ed8db1660c
msgid "`Methodic Configurator <https://github.com/ArduPilot/MethodicConfigurator>`__: if you have your own hardware, this is our recommended setup and configuration tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:50
#: 7df746cf96d1414b83d07cc633a8235c
msgid "Please note that having existing PRs or solving issues is not a requirement for GSoC, and we do not track issue counts. If you are interested, please feel free to work on a few open items for your own learning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:52
#: 43fa1e125bf84fe1982e329b38601a54
msgid "Do not ask to be assigned an issue or ask how or where to contribute. Please follow ArduPilot standards for commit quality, code style, and comments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gsoc.rst:54
#: a91da73b4a2c41bfab757ced404f20be
msgid "If you'd like to discuss your project or ask questions, please create a thread in the `#GSOC category on the ArduPilot forum <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/google-summer-of-code>`__. Please read the pinned message there before posting."
msgstr ""
